WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.887
What about people working remotely?

2
00:00:01.887 --> 00:00:06.900
Take Microsoft's Global Secure Access,
which includes Entra Private Access.

3
00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:09.570
You list your private DNS suffixes,

4
00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:13.712
and its client on the laptop
turns them into NRPT rules.

5
00:00:13.712 --> 00:00:17.490
Matching queries go to a DNS
proxy at Microsoft's edge,

6
00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:22.813
and a connector inside your network
resolves them against on-premises DNS.

7
00:00:22.813 --> 00:00:25.473
The laptop gets back a
synthetic IP address,

8
00:00:25.473 --> 00:00:27.987
a stand-in that routes through the tunnel.

9
00:00:27.987 --> 00:00:31.838
Notice what's missing: that's all
about the laptop finding names.

10
00:00:31.838 --> 00:00:35.973
I found no primary source
saying Global Secure Access

11
00:00:35.973 --> 00:00:40.200
registers the laptop's own
name or address in agency DNS.

12
00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:45.800
So, as an inference, remote clients are
resolvers of names, not registrants.

13
00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:49.700
Windows also skips dynamic
update over VPN by default.

14
00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:52.575
Third-party VPN products
weren't researched.

15
00:00:52.575 --> 00:00:55.850
That changes how the help
desk finds a remote device.

16
00:00:55.850 --> 00:00:59.519
Intune's Remote Help starts
from the Intune admin center:

17
00:00:59.519 --> 00:01:03.813
you pick the device from the device
list, and no DNS lookup is needed.

18
00:01:03.813 --> 00:01:06.100
But you pick it by its Intune device name.

19
00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:09.763
As an inference, that name
must be unique and meaningful.

20
00:01:09.763 --> 00:01:13.107
One subtlety: renaming in the
admin center doesn't change

21
00:01:13.107 --> 00:01:16.451
the management name or the name
in the Company Portal app.

22
00:01:16.451 --> 00:01:24.161
Sources: Microsoft Learn: Understand
Microsoft Entra Private DNS and Troubleshoot

23
00:01:24.161 --> 00:01:30.110
application access (Global Secure
Access) [S51]; Dynamic update [S26];

24
00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:37.161
DirectAccess known issues (NRPT) [S56];
Using Remote Help with Microsoft Intune

25
00:01:37.161 --> 00:01:43.610
